                                                "sense_id": "5c0b96e7-35d3-3cd5-bfb6-49c6211df007",
                                                "text": "It was just plain stupid."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e711b11e-499f-4332-ae93-18bf6ea10918",
                                                "sense_id": "5c0b96e7-35d3-3cd5-bfb6-49c6211df007",
                                                "text": "I plain forgot."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e13f9a57-fb44-35df-ac26-0cf996d8fb47",
                                        "entry_id": "bcdd2f43-e331-3cc4-91a2-8570a9d6fe23",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Plainly; distinctly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e7402ae-5047-43b8-8079-c4a186a22201",
                                                "sense_id": "e13f9a57-fb44-35df-ac26-0cf996d8fb47",
                                                "text": "Tell me plain: do you love me or no?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "plain",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc859d23-9961-3bdb-9115-51550ab80a0e",
                                        "entry_id": "f7bd1f73-d883-364a-a063-78334ae60331",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An expanse of land with relatively low relief and few trees, especially a grassy expanse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b598139a-50eb-480d-8845-7c8b080a9364",
                                                "sense_id": "dc859d23-9961-3bdb-9115-51550ab80a0e",
                                                "text": "Him the Ammonite / Worshipped in Rabba and her watery plain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ec37933-2fa2-441c-b635-cce99a5ef9e3",
                                                "sense_id": "dc859d23-9961-3bdb-9115-51550ab80a0e",
                                                "text": "1961, J. A. Philip. Mimesis in the Sophistês of Plato. In: Proceedings and Transactions of the American Philological Association 92. p. 467.\nFor Plato the life of the philosopher is a life of struggle towards the goal of knowledge, towards “searching the heavens and measuring the plains, in all places seeking the nature of everything as a whole”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d5861432-ef7a-34e8-8fdf-e8eeb7270b0d",
                                        "entry_id": "f7bd1f73-d883-364a-a063-78334ae60331",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A broad, flat expanse in general, as of water."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5774963-2704-46ab-a7b8-20958c48cf01",
                                                "sense_id": "d5861432-ef7a-34e8-8fdf-e8eeb7270b0d",
                                                "text": "Fair ship, that from the Italian shore,\n⁠Sailest the placid ocean-plains\n⁠With my lost Arthur’s loved remains,\nSpread thy full wings, and waft him o’er."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f1bf2207-e5c2-3e5d-851a-511a81d11876",
                                        "entry_id": "f7bd1f73-d883-364a-a063-78334ae60331",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of field in reference to a battlefield."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd99c2a9-6270-491a-90c0-09d905fa2e3e",
                                                "sense_id": "f1bf2207-e5c2-3e5d-851a-511a81d11876",
                                                "text": "You have stormed no town and found the money there ; neither did you find it in the plains of Plassey after the defeat of the Nawab"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de84e662-525c-45f1-85bc-5aab835edfe9",
                                                "sense_id": "f1bf2207-e5c2-3e5d-851a-511a81d11876",
                                                "text": "Lead forth my soldiers to the plain."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b9e8b3a9-5d27-39fe-8c5c-e4dbc5419904",
                                        "entry_id": "f7bd1f73-d883-364a-a063-78334ae60331",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of plane: a flat geometric field."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "plain",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f133e83c-7449-37dc-9b3e-36538bde8e9e",
                                        "entry_id": "701df833-085f-32fa-a18f-b4e98ffe3326",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To level; to raze; to make plain or even on the surface."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f48cb9b0-859f-4762-af31-259362b4be5c",
                                                "sense_id": "f133e83c-7449-37dc-9b3e-36538bde8e9e",
                                                "text": "Frownst thou thereat aspiring Lancaster,\nThe sworde shall plane the furrowes of thy browes,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3a88820-2495-4907-9f9f-893573aee105",
                                                "sense_id": "f133e83c-7449-37dc-9b3e-36538bde8e9e",
                                                "text": "We would rake Europe rather, plain the East;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d3bb20dc-6456-30e9-aea2-d353a83c7cd8",
                                        "entry_id": "701df833-085f-32fa-a18f-b4e98ffe3326",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make plain or manifest; to explain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50914e45-cd2a-4a74-a0e8-8b2504345567",
                                                "sense_id": "d3bb20dc-6456-30e9-aea2-d353a83c7cd8",
                                                "text": "What’s dumb in show, I’ll plain with speech."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "plain",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b15ce6d0-01ed-3db6-9390-df3e2860d0d6",
                                        "entry_id": "0bdafea1-c1e0-3382-be93-5cbbe00d2d1c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lamentation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "poetic",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23f7dc25-365a-42c7-a027-06eeef0b544b",
                                                "sense_id": "b15ce6d0-01ed-3db6-9390-df3e2860d0d6",
                                                "text": "The warrior-threat, the infant's plain,\nThe mother's screams, were heard in vain;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "plain",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c77bdfdd-2f40-305f-b94a-b6079fcaf528",
                                        "entry_id": "04b14a45-f2fc-33e0-b868-cf4dc81e6a0e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To complain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "reflexive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8213f8fe-6fae-4e3a-9a90-e245f92c5b57",
                                                "sense_id": "c77bdfdd-2f40-305f-b94a-b6079fcaf528",
                                                "text": "Persones and parisch prestes · pleyned hem to þe bischop / Þat here parisshes were pore · sith þe pestilence tyme […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ecd65e90-0f28-3982-8b5e-99809d2611c4",
                                        "entry_id": "04b14a45-f2fc-33e0-b868-cf4dc81e6a0e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To lament, bewail."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive",
                                            "archaic",
                                            "poetic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65dd096b-214c-4488-8190-e7d6c4d19aae",
                                                "sense_id": "ecd65e90-0f28-3982-8b5e-99809d2611c4",
                                                "text": "to plain a loss"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81b6c1d6-5289-4685-831d-802532d87d6b",
                                                "sense_id": "ecd65e90-0f28-3982-8b5e-99809d2611c4",
                                                "text": "Shepheards, that wont[…]\nOft times to plaine your loves concealed smart"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f94a6e1e-4a94-4c36-a70d-7955fc35718c",
                                                "sense_id": "ecd65e90-0f28-3982-8b5e-99809d2611c4",
                                                "text": "Thy mother could thee for thy cradle set\nHer husband's rusty iron corselet;\nWhose jargling sound might rock her babe to rest,\nThat never plain'd of his uneasy nest."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7594f9ef-84f1-4fa4-92c0-8b13716a4266",
                                                "sense_id": "ecd65e90-0f28-3982-8b5e-99809d2611c4",
                                                "text": "Then, again, she almost thought that the soft and wailing wind which swept mournfully through the sepulchral boughs of the large old yews, had a voice not of this world—was it the inarticulate plaining of her brother's gentle spirit, debarred from intercourse, but still keeping over her the deep and eternal watch of love?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e49767f2-a633-44b5-af7f-ea6e18f4a60d",
                                                "sense_id": "ecd65e90-0f28-3982-8b5e-99809d2611c4",
                                                "text": "Then came I crying, and to-day, / With heavier cause to plain, / Depart I into death away, / Not to be born again."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "plain",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "adc89d78-4c59-3ef8-b664-2020e58efe28",
                                        "entry_id": "0f497d5c-50f5-3ae2-b4ca-e2c26aab5e72",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Full, complete in number or extent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
